dsh-pet's /broadcast can put a picture in the bubble: a meme by its name, looked up in the
pet's meme directories on disk (host/memes.ts, Node's fs), or any http or https address. A-NAS
serves none of dsh-pet's meme pictures, and a picture from an address would put whatever it
points at on the member's screen, the host's shared screen included. VNAS's broadcast tool has
neither and the product service drops both, so the page's decision refuses either as
bad-request; it no longer imports memes.ts or needs the meme directories. The text, duration
and anim rules and the pet check are unchanged.

